# Netlify Redirects — Haus Fund (haus.fund)

# Redirect www to apex
https://www.haus.fund/* https://haus.fund/:splat 301!
https://www.haus.fund https://haus.fund 301!

# The mentor network is members-only.
#
# It used to be a public page at /mentors, rendered from the Airtable Mentors
# table. Homeroom already has a mentor directory behind its sign-in, so this
# sends both paths there rather than adding a second gate: whoever is signed in
# gets the directory, whoever is not gets the Homeroom sign-in page.
#
# Forced, because publish = "." would otherwise serve a file at /mentors.html
# straight past the redirect. 302 rather than 301: a permanent redirect is
# cached hard by browsers, and this is a policy that could be reversed.
#
# The /api/mentors edge function that fed the old page is gone from
# netlify.toml. Hiding the page while leaving the JSON open would have moved
# the front door without locking it.
/mentors /homeroom/mentors 302!
/mentors.html /homeroom/mentors 302!

# Internal docs live in the repo for reference but must not be served.
# publish = "." means every committed file is otherwise reachable.
#
# These must be listed one per file and forced with "!". A wildcard does not
# work here: Netlify only allows a splat at the END of a path, so "/*.md" never
# matches, and without "!" an existing static file wins over the redirect.
#
# ADDING A NEW .md TO THIS REPO? Add a line here too, or it goes live.
/README.md /404.html 404!
/DEPLOYMENT.md /404.html 404!
/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md /404.html 404!
/SKILL.md /404.html 404!
/CONNECT-GIT.md /404.html 404!
/tools/core-facility-finder/SKILL.md /404.html 404!
/tools/core-facility-finder/README.md /404.html 404!
/tools/visa-letter-generator/README.md /404.html 404!
/tools/biopunk-skill-tree/README.md /404.html 404!
/netlify/functions/news/README.md /404.html 404!

# The news app's source and tests live under netlify/ and are covered by the
# rule below. Its stylesheet and client script are served from /news-assets.

# Edge-function source lives in the repo and would otherwise be served as a
# static file, because publish = ".". No secrets are in it (the LP password is
# an environment variable), but it is not part of the site.
/netlify/* /404.html 404!

# Supabase migrations and config live in the repo and describe the database
# schema and its RLS policies. No secrets are in them — the keys are Netlify
# environment variables — but there is no reason to serve them either.
/supabase/* /404.html 404!

# No catch-all. Unknown paths fall through to 404.html with a real 404 status.
# A "/* /index.html 200" rule here would turn every typo into a soft 404: the
# homepage served under a 200, which search engines penalise and users misread.
